[0.256, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  (another command ran in this repository at the same time; a change made by either may show under either \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bresult)\u001b[14G\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mSea\u001b[7Gched for \u001b[1m9\u001b[22m patterns, read \u001b[1m15\u001b[22m files, listed \u001b[1m3\u001b[22m directories, ran \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \r\u001b[2B●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mAnswered Claude's questions:\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · Where should the client's pinned server keys live? (Format either way: YAML through Jettison's archive, `version:\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m1`, `servers: [{endpoint: \"host:port\", key: <64 hex>}]`, read at each `connect`.) → Bundle + user override \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(Recommended)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· How is a key matched \u001b[30Go\u001b[32Ga server at connect? → E\u001b[57Gact host:por\u001b[71G(Recomme\u001b[80Gd\u001b[82Gd)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mBoth recommended options chosen. Setting up lane B and reading the standards, the\u001b[85Gdocs\u001b[90Gto\u001b[93Gchange\u001b[100Gand\u001b[104Gthe\u001b[108Gpin.\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mSearched for \u001b[1m14\u001b[22m patterns, read \u001b[1m13\u001b[22m files, listed \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m directory, ran \u001b[1m5\u001b[22m shell commands \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mFound an engine gap: \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mWriteFileDurably\u001b[39m always creates files 0644, so a 0600 key file\u001b[87Gneeds\u001b[93Ga\u001b[95Gpermissions\u001b[107Gparameter\u001b[117Gin\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BJettison.\u001b[13GMaking\u001b[20Gthat\u001b[25Gsmall\u001b[31Gengine\u001b[38Gchange\u001b[45Gin\u001b[48G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mjettison.lane