[0.020, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[40C\u001b[14B…\u001b[K\r\u001b[27C\u001b[4B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;235;159;127mKe\u001b[38;2;215;119;87mrfuffling…\u001b[39m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.016, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[2m 147 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 148 \u001b[22m `connect <host:port> <token>` plays on a dedicated server ([\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mthe server\u001b[39m](server.md)) as the\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 149 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mtoken's actor. A failed connect keeps the connection there was; a new one replaces it. While          \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m 150 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mconnected:                                                                                            \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 149 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mtoken's actor, pinning the server's key from the                                                      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 150 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m[\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mserver list\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m](server.md#connections-are-sealed); an endpoint the list does not name is refused,       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 151 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mand a server that does not hold the pinned key ends in `Disconnected from ...: key mismatch.`. A      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 152 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mfailed connect keeps the connection there was; a new one replaces it. While connected:                \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m 153 \u001b[12G\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 154 \u001b[12G\u001b[22m-\u001b[14GThe\u001b[18Gplayers'\u001b[27Gcommands\u001b[36Gdrop\u001b[41Gthe\u001b[45Gprincipal\u001b[55Gargument,\u001b[65Gsince\u001b[71Gthe\u001b[75Gactor\u001b[81Gis\u001b[84Gthe\u001b[88Gtoken's.\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m 155 \u001b[22m   `provision` needs an administrator's token.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[39m Docs are done. Waiting for the build.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mMake a note, you are allowed to write code, and run an incremental build on it while the gate runs on another \u001b[39m        \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mworktree. You may even run lightweight testing. What is not allowed to happen is for two gates to run at the same \u001b[39m    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mtime if they are heavy gates.\u001b[39m                                                                                         \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mRecalling \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m memory, searching\u001b[33Gmemories…\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[0.170, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[40C\u001b[20B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
