[0.451, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mSaved\u001b[10Go memory:\u001b[22m never\u001b[26Grun\u001b[30Gtwo\u001b[34Gheavy\u001b[40Ggates\u001b[46Gat\u001b[49Gonce.\u001b[55GCode\u001b[60Gedits,\u001b[67Gincremental\u001b[79Gbuilds\u001b[86Gand\u001b[90Glight\u001b[96Gtests\u001b[102Gare\u001b[106Gfine\u001b[111Gbeside\u001b[118Ga\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bgate in another lane. This replaces\u001b[39Gthe\u001b[43Gold\u001b[47G\"nothing beside\u001b[63Gclang\" note.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mOne devia\u001b[13Gion from the handoff.\u001b[22m Jettison's durable write a\u001b[62Gways created files as 0644,\u001b[90Gso\u001b[93Gthe\u001b[97Gserver's\u001b[106Gsecret\u001b[113Gkey\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcould never be 0600 from the moment it was written. I added a pe\u001b[68Gmissions parameter to \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mCore::WriteFileDurably\u001b[39m;\u001b[114Gthe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bdefault stays 0644. It also now replaces a\u001b[47Gartial file left\u001b[64Gby a crash inst\u001b[80Gad of\u001b[86Greusing it, si\u001b[101Gc\u001b[103G reusing it\u001b[115Gwould\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bkeep th\u001b[11G old mode. This\u001b[27Gis\u001b[30Gin\u001b[33G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mjettison.lane-b\u001b[39m,\u001b[50Gbranch\u001b[57G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mprivate-durable-files\u001b[39m,\u001b[80Grecorded\u001b[89Gin\u001b[92Gthe\u001b[96Gengine's\u001b[105Ghistory\u001b[113Gand\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mpersistence.md\u001b[39m. So Manifest has to\u001b[38Gbe pinned to that engine commit rather\u001b[77Gthan \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m24bd3ec\u001b[39m;\u001b[91Gth\u001b[94G dev\u001b[99Gshell files\u001b[111Ghaven't\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bchanged.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mWhere things stand:\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mEngine:\u001b[22m the \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mcore\u001b[39m suite has a\u001b[34Gtest for the 0600 write, and the fu\u001b[70Gl 