ane-c\u001b[63G\u001b[39m(branch\u001b[71G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mcomment-spacing\u001b[39m):\u001b[89Gthe\u001b[93Gscript\u001b[100Gpass,\u001b[106Gthe\u001b[110Grule\u001b[115Gin\u001b[118Gthe\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bcoding\u001b[12Gstandards,\u001b[23Gand\u001b[27G1,264\u001b[33Gblank\u001b[39Glines\u001b[45Gin\u001b[48G258\u001b[52Gfiles.\u001b[59G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mcomment-only.sh\u001b[75G\u001b[39mand\u001b[79Gthe\u001b[83Gformat\u001b[90Gcheck\u001b[96Gpass.\u001b[102GNot\u001b[106Gcommitted.\u001b[117GIt\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G  still needs a run of the\u001b[30Gdeclara\u001b[38Gion pass\u001b[47Gagain\u001b[53Gt\u001b[55Glane-c's own build, and then Ma\u001b[87Gifest with \u001b[38;2;177;185;249m--root\u001b[39m once the\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  en\u001b[8Gryption branc\u001b[22G has merged.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3GHow s\u001b[9Gould I handle the red gate?\u001b[37G\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  1. \u001b[1mRecommended:\u001b[22m fix \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mfeature-base\u001b[39m first, as its own commit on this branch. That means\u001b[88Gthe\u001b[92Gwater\u001b[98Gprice\u001b[104G(data\u001b[110Gor\u001b[113GD-093's\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Btest),\u001b[13Gwhy\u001b[17Gthe\u001b[21Gdevelopment\u001b[33Gfixture's\u001b[43Gask\u001b[47Gis\u001b[50G0,\u001b[53Gthen\u001b[58Gre-pinning\u001b[69Gthe\u001b[73Ghashes\u001b[80Gonce\u001b[85GI've\u001b[90Gshown\u001b[96Gthey\u001b[101Gmove\u001b[106Gonly\u001b[111Gfor\u001b[115Gthe\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G   content. Then commit and push encryption on a green gate.\r\u001b[1B  2.\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
